# suite TSTRUTIL
ok 1 - D-21 a lower case item code is stored upper case
ok 2 - folding to upper case is reported as a change
ok 3 - D-21 underscore and full stop are allowed
ok 4 - D-21 a space inside a code is rejected
ok 5 - D-21 an ampersand is rejected and located
ok 6 - D-21 forty characters are allowed
ok 7 - D-21 forty one characters are rejected
ok 8 - a shorter limit can be imposed (20 for parties)
ok 9 - an empty code is rejected
ok 10 - SI-000123 normalises to SI123 under STRIP
ok 11 - si 000123 normalises to the same thing
ok 12 - SI/000123 normalises to the same thing
ok 13 - KEEP leaves the leading zeros in place
ok 14 - an all zero number keeps one digit
ok 15 - a purely numeric reference still normalises
ok 16 - COM-004 SI123 and SI1234 stay different
ok 17 - a reference with no letters or digits is rejected
ok 18 - money defaults to GBP 1,234.56
ok 19 - the pound symbol is a single X'A3' byte on request
ok 20 - the symbol form is nine characters long
ok 21 - a negative amount keeps its sign
ok 22 - a foreign currency names itself
ok 23 - zero formats as GBP 0.00, not blank
ok 24 - millions are grouped correctly
ok 25 - a quantity keeps six decimals by default
ok 26 - trailing zeros can be trimmed for display
ok 27 - a whole quantity trims to no decimal point at all
ok 28 - a six decimal quantity is never rounded away
ok 29 - UPPER folds mixed case text
ok 30 - SQUEEZE collapses runs of spaces
ok 31 - an unknown function is rejected (STR0009)
1..31
# TSTRUTIL passed 00031 failed 00000
# exit 0
